<%# locals: (href:, name:, detail: nil, badge: nil, warning: nil) %>
<%# One thing in a list that's opened by choosing it, such as a CSV format or an Account: its name, with an optional muted line under it saying more, an optional `badge`, a short word beside the name that says what it is, such as Inactive, and an optional `warning`, a few words beside it that say it needs a second look, such as "Needs reconnecting" (components/warning_badge). The whole row links to where it's opened. Put rows in components/record_list. %>
<li>
  <%= link_to href, class: "list-row hover:bg-base-200" do %>
    <span class="list-col-grow">
      <span class="block font-semibold"><%= name %><% if badge %> <%= render "components/label_badge", text: badge %><% end %><% if warning %> <%= render "components/warning_badge", text: warning %><% end %></span>
      <% if detail.present? %>
        <span class="block text-base-content/70"><%= detail %></span>
      <% end %>
    </span>
  <% end %>
</li>
